  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wider and results-driven Government-CSO dialogue is promoted through regional and national mechanisms</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="263608" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wider and results-driven Government-CSO dialogue is promoted through regional and national mechanisms</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2016-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2016-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="25 programmes monitored by the CSOs"></target>
     <actual value="- Coalition of 27 CSOs monitored the progress achieved throughout implementation of 25 regional programmes for fostering civil society development. and/or advocated for their adoption (report prepared and presented in public 2014). 
- Civil society mapping research conducted. a national conference on civil society and state cooperation organized (300 participants); and a revision of a National Strategy on Civil Society Development was launched (2015). 
- 4 subnational programmes on CSO development were elaborated with CSO inputs. and monitored by the CSOs (in Kherson. Dnipro. Zakarpattia. and Donetsk oblasts): 1) 46 information meetings on the Strategy for 1.336 local CSOs&#x2019; representatives. local government officials. and MPs were conducted; 2) 4 subnational programmes were developed. out of all of them 3 were approved. and 3) Coordination Councils for strategy implementation in pilot oblasts were created; one more programme is pending approval of its oblast council (2016)."></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2017-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2017-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Udskudt til 2018"></target>
     <actual value="N/A"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
