  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Selected regional civil society organisations have increased organisational capacities to serve as regional capacity-building hubs</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="263607" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Selected regional civil society organisations have increased organisational capacities to serve as regional capacity-building hubs</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2016-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2016-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="9 organisations have increased organisational capacities to serve as regional capacity-building hubs"></target>
     <actual value="8* mid-size regional CSOs serve as capacity-building hubs human rights and good governance: 
&#x2022;	Hubs strengthened their positions as regional leaders among local CSOs - almost 2.600 CSO representatives and local authorities have benefited from capacity building initiatives implemented by hubs; 
&#x2022;	Hubs reformed their system of governance according to the principles of democratic governance. improved planning and management systems and control over internal processes in organizations; 
&#x2022;	Hubs moved toward openness and transparency in their organisations&#x2019; activities; 
